# Corporate Knowledge Base Architecture Plan

## Executive Summary
This document outlines the strategic restructuring of our enterprise Knowledge Base (KB). The goal is to maximize self-service enablement, decrease duplicate content by 40%, and reduce customer support ticket volumes by routing users to verified, structurally sound technical solutions.

## Core Hierarchy & Information Architecture
The KB is organized into four main functional pillars to support internal support engineers, external DevOps clients, and standard system administrators.

```text
Root Tier (Enterprise Cloud Platform)
├── 01-Onboarding-and-Licensing (User Persona: Global Admins)
│   ├── Getting Started Guides
│   └── License Activation & True-Up Guides
├── 02-Core-Infrastructure (User Persona: Cloud Architects)
│   ├── Compute Provisioning
│   └── Network Topology & VPC Peering
├── 03-Security-and-Compliance (User Persona: InfoSec Officers)
│   ├── Identity Governance (IAM)
│   └── Audit Logging & Audit Trails
└── 04-Developer-Resources (User Persona: Systems Engineers)
    ├── SDK Reference Links
    └── Webhook Integration Modules
```

## Article Metadata Standards
To maintain cross-platform indexing capabilities, every knowledge base article must include the following YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
id: KB-10825
title: Troubleshooting Asynchronous Database Connection Pools Timeout
author: Dhara Gohil
created_date: 2026-11-01
last_reviewed: 2026-11-01
audience: [devops-engineers, tier-3-support]
products: [cloud-broker-v2]
lifecycle_status: verified
tags: [database, clustering, connection-pool]
```
